[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> response_text: `Okay, so I have this problem where I need to find the real solutions to the equation f(x) = f(-x) for the function f. The function f is defined for all real numbers except x = 0. The given equation is f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x. Hmm, interesting.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Alright, let me try to figure this out step by step. I remember that when there's a functional equation like this, often substituting x with 1/x can help create another equation that can be solved together with the original one. Let me try that.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> So, the original equation is:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x.  [Equation 1]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> If I substitute x with 1/x in this equation, I should get:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> f(1/x) + 2f(x) = 3*(1/x).  [Equation 2]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Now, I have two equations:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 1) f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 2) f(1/x) + 2f(x) = 3/x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> I need to solve for f(x) and f(1/x). Let me treat these as a system of linear equations in terms of f(x) and f(1/x). Let me denote f(x) as A and f(1/x) as B for simplicity.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> So, Equation 1 becomes:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> A + 2B = 3x.  [Equation 1a]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Equation 2 becomes:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> B + 2A = 3/x.  [Equation 2a]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Now, I can write this as a system of equations:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> A + 2B = 3x   ...(1a)
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 2A + B = 3/x   ...(2a)  [I rearranged Equation 2a to standard form]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Wait, actually, Equation 2a is B + 2A = 3/x, which is the same as 2A + B = 3/x.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> So, the system is:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 1) A + 2B = 3x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 2) 2A + B = 3/x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> I need to solve for A (which is f(x)) and B (which is f(1/x)).
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Let me use the method of elimination. Let me multiply Equation 1 by 2 to make the coefficient of A equal to 2, then subtract Equation 2 from it.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Multiply Equation 1 by 2:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 2A + 4B = 6x.  [Equation 3]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Now, subtract Equation 2 from Equation 3:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> (2A + 4B) - (2A + B) = 6x - (3/x)
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> Simplify:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,693 >> 2A + 4B - 2A - B = 6x - 3/x`
