[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> Response: `Okay, so I have this problem where I need to find the real solutions to the equation f(x) = f(-x) for the function f. The function f is defined for all real numbers except x = 0. The given equation is f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x. Hmm, interesting.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> Alright, let me try to figure this out step by step. I remember that when there's a functional equation like this, often substituting x with 1/x can help create another equation that can be solved together with the original one. Let me try that.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> So, the original equation is:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x.  [Equation 1]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> If I substitute x with 1/x in this equation, I should get:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> f(1/x) + 2f(x) = 3*(1/x).  [Equation 2]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> Now, I have two equations:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 1) f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 2) f(1/x) + 2f(x) = 3/x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> I need to solve for f(x) and f(1/x). Let me treat these as a system of linear equations in terms of f(x) and f(1/x). Let me denote f(x) as A and f(1/x) as B for simplicity.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> So, Equation 1 becomes:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> A + 2B = 3x.  [Equation 1a]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> Equation 2 becomes:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> B + 2A = 3/x.  [Equation 2a]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,694 >> Now, I can write this as a system of equations:
