[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,737 >> First step is to see how many times the leading term of the divisor, which is \(x^2\), goes into the leading term of the dividend, which is \(2x^4\). So, \(2x^4 / x^2 = 2x^2\). That means the first term in the quotient will be \(2x^2\). 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,737 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:178:275] 2026-10-26 20:23:38,737 >> Now, I multiply the entire divisor by \(2x^2\): \(2x^2 \times (x^2 + 7x -5) = 2x^4 + 14x^3 -10x^2\). 
