[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> Okay, so I have this problem where I need to find the real solutions to the equation f(x) = f(-x) for the function f. The function f is defined for all real numbers except x = 0. The given equation is f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x. Hmm, interesting.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> Alright, let me try to figure this out step by step. I remember that when there's a functional equation like this, often substituting x with 1/x can help create another equation that can be solved together with the original one. Let me try that.
