[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> So, the original equation is:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x.  [Equation 1]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> If I substitute x with 1/x in this equation, I should get:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> f(1/x) + 2f(x) = 3*(1/x).  [Equation 2]
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> Now, I have two equations:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> 1) f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3287] 2026-10-26 20:28:20,984 >> 2) f(1/x) + 2f(x) = 3/x
