[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Alright, let me think. When the tank is 7/8 full, subtracting 12 gallons brings it down to half full. So, the difference between 7/8 and 1/2 must be equal to the 12 gallons used. That makes sense because using 12 gallons reduces the full capacity by 7/8 - 1/2.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Let me write that down as an equation. Let's let x be the total capacity of the tank in gallons. So, 7/8 of x minus 12 gallons equals 1/2 of x. So, the equation is:
