[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> (7/8)x - 12 = (1/2)x
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Now, I need to solve for x. Let me subtract (1/2)x from both sides to get all the x terms on one side. 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> (7/8)x - (1/2)x - 12 = 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> But wait, actually, moving the (1/2)x to the left, it would be:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> (7/8)x - (1/2)x = 12
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Now, I can subtract these fractions. To subtract 1/2 from 7/8, I need a common denominator. 8 is the common denominator, right? So 1/2 is equal to 4/8. Subtracting 4/8 from 7/8 gives 3/8. So,
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> (3/8)x = 12
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Now, to solve for x, I can multiply both sides by the reciprocal of 3/8, which is 8/3.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> x = 12 * (8/3)
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Let me compute that. 12 divided by 3 is 4, and 4 multiplied by 8 is 32. So, x equals 32.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:3287] 2026-10-26 20:32:42,563 >> Wait, let me double-check that. If the full capacity is 32 gallons, then 7/8 of that is 28 gallons. Subtracting 12 gallons gives 16 gallons, which is half of 32. Oh, yeah, that makes sense. So, 32 is the correct answer.
